  "needs": {"container": true, "reason": "Most Java dependencies carry no version in the project: the starters, postgresql, micrometer-registry-stackdriver, junit-jupiter-engine (through ${junit-jupiter.version}) and spring-boot-maven-plugin take theirs from the external parent spring-boot-starter-parent 3.5.16 and from four imported BOMs (spring-cloud-gcp-dependencies 5.13.11, spring-cloud-dependencies 2025.1.3 through ${spring-cloud.version}, libraries-bom 26.88.1, micrometer-bom 1.17.1, the last absent from ledgermonolith). Only the effective POM of each module, which downloads them, states the classpath. The Python and Terraform facts read from the files."},
  "unknown": [{"facet": "dependencies", "known": ["frontend", "loadgenerator", "iac/tf-anthos-gke"]}],
  "traps": [
    "The four Java modules inherit groupId org.springframework.boot from their parent spring-boot-starter-parent, so they are org.springframework.boot:ledgerwriter and so on, not com.google.cloud.anthos.samples:*; the root pom.xml only aggregates them (<modules>) and is nobody's parent, so its pluginManagement (jib 3.5.2, maven-compiler-plugin 3.16.0 with -Xlint:all, jacoco 0.8.15) reaches none of them and depends_on is empty everywhere",
    "There is no shared Java library: ledgerwriter, balancereader, transactionhistory and ledgermonolith each carry their own Transaction, TransactionRepository, JWTVerifierGenerator (and LedgerReader where present) with the same names; ledgermonolith re-implements the three ledger services in one Spring Boot application and has no src/test",
    "The Java images are built by jib-maven-plugin from eclipse-temurin:17.0.4.1_1-jre-alpine written in each pom, not from a Dockerfile; skaffold drives jib through the root mvnw (../../../mvnw), while ledgermonolith is a jar copied to Cloud Storage and run by a GCE startup script that downloads OpenJDK 17.0.1",
    "transactionhistory's spring-boot-maven-plugin names mainClass anthos.samples.bankofanthos.transactionhistory.TransActionHistoryApplication; the class is TransactionHistoryApplication",
    "lettuce-core 7.7.0.RELEASE (a Redis client) is declared by all four poms and used by no code; there is no Redis anywhere",
    "application.properties sets spring.sleuth.* although no Sleuth dependency is declared (Spring Boot 3); tracing comes from spring-cloud-gcp-starter-trace",
    "The four Python services are uv projects without [build-system] (virtual, installed with uv sync --no-install-project); there is no requirements.txt and no uv workspace: each has its own pyproject.toml, uv.lock and .python-version",
    "userservice and contacts list in [project].dependencies about 47 packages copied from an old freeze (attrs, certifi, idna, py, pluggy, zipp ...): most are transitive in reality, and contacts pins pyjwt>=2.10.1 and urllib3>=2.6.3 where userservice says 2.12.0 and 2.6.0",
    "The Python services import their own modules flat (from db import UserDb) through pytest pythonpath = ['.'], while the tests import the service folder as a package (from contacts.contacts import create_app), which works only because the folder has __init__.py and pytest puts its parent on sys.path",
    "accounts-db and ledger-db are PostgreSQL 16.15 images with init SQL and shell scripts copied to /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d; accounts-db/initdb/1-load-testdata.sql is copied by no Dockerfile and read by no script",
    "kubernetes-manifests/ is the release output of docs/releasing/make-release.sh (skaffold render per module, image tags v0.6.11); the deployable sources are the kustomize bases and overlays under src/*/k8s, src/components and iac/acm-multienv-cicd-anthos-autopilot, driven by skaffold.yaml and its required configs",
    "docs/ is not only documentation: docs/releasing/make-release.sh and docs/releasing/header.txt are run by .github/workflows/make-release.yaml",
    "The Cypress e2e tests have no package.json: cypress comes from the cypress/included:13.17.0 image in .github/workflows/ui-tests/Dockerfile, while the Makefile test-e2e target runs cypress/included:5.0.0",
    "pgpool.py exists twice: as a file in extras/postgres-hpa/helm-postgres-ha/pgpool-operator and inlined in the ConfigMap of extras/postgres-hpa/kubernetes-manifests/pgpool-operator.yaml, whose python:3.13 container runs pip3 install kopf kubernetes at start: no file declares those dependencies",
    "iac/tf-anthos-gke uses resource time_sleep, whose provider hashicorp/time is not in required_providers; neither Terraform root has a .terraform.lock.hcl, and iac/tf-multienv-cicd-anthos-autopilot declares no required_version (the CI runs whatever terraform the runner has)",
    "Every service address is an environment variable from the ConfigMap service-api-config (kubernetes-manifests/config.yaml, iac/acm-multienv-cicd-anthos-autopilot/base/config.yaml); src/ledgermonolith/config.yaml points TRANSACTIONS, BALANCES and HISTORY at the monolith on a GCE VM, so the same frontend call reaches different units",
    "The Spring services read their database from SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL in ledger-db-config with no line of code; userservice and contacts read ACCOUNTS_DB_URI from accounts-db-config",
    "The frontend is one unit with three parts: the Flask server, Jinja templates and browser JavaScript in static/scripts; Bootstrap Material Design, jQuery and Popper come from unpkg and code.jquery.com links in templates/shared, not from any manifest",
    "The two ledger readers learn about new transactions only by polling the TRANSACTIONS table (LedgerReader), not by any call from ledgerwriter",
    "The jwt-secret.yaml files (extras/jwt, extras/cloudsql/kubernetes-manifests, iac/acm-multienv-cicd-anthos-autopilot/base) hold the RSA key pair used to sign and verify tokens and are not read for this fixture"
  ],
